``` KV-10 | Authentication Tokens: Created, Used, Expiring
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: Audit Splunk authentication tokens: who created them, which are
    unused or never expire, which belong to disabled users, and when each was
    last used.
    Run on: SH-local. Tokens are stored per instance; in an SHC they replicate
    across members.
    Query: Token creation and deletion history (SH)
    If this returns nothing, run probes/KV-10-probe.spl,
    probes/KV-10-probe-rest.spl to confirm the data it reads exists here.
    STATUS: lab verification pending; field or message names may differ on your version.
```
index=_internal sourcetype=splunkd_access earliest=-90d
    (method=POST OR method=DELETE) uri="*/authorization/tokens*"
| eval change=if(method="DELETE", "DELETE", "CREATE_OR_UPDATE")
| table _time host user clientip change uri status
| sort 0 - _time
